  "name": "Adiabatic gas pressure coupled to piston mechanics and damping",
  "description": "Uniform gas obeys a reversible adiabatic lumped closure and drives an inertial spring piston. Dissipated mechanical work is tracked outside the gas; no heat is returned to it. No leakage, shocks, wall heat exchange or engine-combustion claim. Illustrative SI volume0.01m3,area0.01m2,mass1kg,spring1000N/m,external damper10kg/s,external100kPa,gamma1.4. Initial displacement0.02m,zero speed,pressure from pV^gamma=100000*0.01^gamma,damper heat0. Horizon2s,RK4step0.0005s. Original mathematical transcription/adaptation; not a calibrated forecast. Signed net-rate flows implement the stated equations. No numerical clamps or hidden resets.",
  "category": "physics",
  "source": "https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/3-6-adiabatic-processes-for-an-ideal-gas",
